WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.137
Every living thing needs energy
to grow, move and stay healthy.

2
00:00:09.357 --> 00:00:13.908
Today you follow it: from the Sun,
into a plant, along a food chain.

3
00:00:14.408 --> 00:00:17.752
Nothing lives without
energy. Growing takes energy.

4
00:00:17.972 --> 00:00:21.826
Moving takes energy. Even
staying warm takes energy.

5
00:00:22.046 --> 00:00:25.297
No energy, no movement.
Nothing at all can happen.

6
00:00:25.517 --> 00:00:29.975
Every living thing must get energy
from somewhere. Where does it start?

7
00:00:30.475 --> 00:00:35.119
Plants get their energy from light.
Their leaves catch the sunlight.

8
00:00:35.339 --> 00:00:40.215
The plant uses it to make food, and
the energy is stored in the plant.

9
00:00:40.435 --> 00:00:45.312
Animals cannot use light. A rabbit
eats the plant and gets the energy.

10
00:00:45.532 --> 00:00:49.061
A fox eats the rabbit, and
the energy moves along again.

11
00:00:49.281 --> 00:00:53.739
The fox is running on sunlight that
came through the plant and the rabbit.

12
00:00:53.959 --> 00:01:00.136
You are the same. Water and air are
needed, but the energy is in your food.

13
00:01:00.636 --> 00:01:06.487
An animal cannot make its own food.
It has to eat: it is a consumer.

14
00:01:06.707 --> 00:01:12.187
A consumer that eats only plants is a
herbivore: a rabbit, a horse, an elephant.

15
00:01:12.407 --> 00:01:17.469
One that eats only animals is a
carnivore: a lion, an owl, a shark.

16
00:01:17.689 --> 00:01:22.472
One that eats both is an omnivore:
a bear, a pig, and most people.

17
00:01:22.692 --> 00:01:27.847
Big does not mean carnivore. The biggest
land animal, the elephant, is a herbivore.

18
00:01:28.347 --> 00:01:33.456
A predator hunts and eats other
animals: an owl, a fox, a shark.

19
00:01:33.676 --> 00:01:38.459
Prey is the animal that gets
hunted. A mouse is the owl's prey.

20
00:01:38.679 --> 00:01:43.927
Prey does not mean small. A zebra
is prey to a lion, and it is huge.

21
00:01:44.147 --> 00:01:48.883
A frog is both at once. It hunts
flies, and a heron hunts the frog.

22
00:01:49.103 --> 00:01:53.422
The plant at the start is neither. It
is the producer, and it gets eaten.

23
00:01:53.922 --> 00:01:58.891
A food chain drawn with arrows is
a model. It shows who eats whom.

24
00:01:59.111 --> 00:02:03.709
Grass comes first: the producer,
with its energy from light.

25
00:02:03.929 --> 00:02:07.366
Then the rabbit: a herbivore,
and the fox's prey.

26
00:02:07.586 --> 00:02:11.301
Then the fox: a consumer,
and a predator in this chain.

27
00:02:11.521 --> 00:02:16.211
Each arrow means eaten by, and it
shows which way the energy goes.

28
00:02:16.431 --> 00:02:20.750
Take the grass away. The rabbits have
nothing to eat, and the chain breaks.

29
00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:25.383
The sea has food chains too,
starting with tiny floating plants.

30
00:02:25.603 --> 00:02:29.272
A small fish eats them:
a herbivore, and prey.

31
00:02:29.492 --> 00:02:33.950
A bigger fish eats the small fish,
and a seal eats the bigger fish.

32
00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:38.814
Start with the producer, always,
and point each arrow at the eater.

33
00:02:39.314 --> 00:02:44.655
Nothing lives without energy. Plants get
it from light; animals get it by eating.

34
00:02:44.875 --> 00:02:51.701
Herbivore, carnivore, omnivore: plants,
animals, both. Predators hunt prey.

35
00:02:51.921 --> 00:02:56.473
A food chain is a model. Its arrows
show which way the energy goes.
